Note that the definition of "home directory" can get 
rather weird when you're operating outside the *nix 
universe.  Windows is not quite as odd as VMS or 
the old (pre-X) MacOS, but you'll still find different 
software making different assumptions about what 
constitutes your "home directory".  Some things will
use your Documents folder, but others will use its
parent directory (the one named for your user account; 
the default path to it varies significantly depending 
which version of Windows you have).  I don't happen 
to know what NetHack does in that regard on Windows.

